r</surname><given-names>UV</given-names></name><name><surname>Hediger</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Tubular localization and tissue distribution of peptide transporters in rat kidney.</article-title><source>Pharm Res</source><volume>15</volume><fpage>1244</fpage><lpage>1249</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9706056</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002476-Ogihara2"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ogihara</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Suzuki</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Nagamachi</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Inui</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Takata</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Peptide transporter in the rat small intestine: ultrastructural localization and the effect of starvation and administration of amino acids.</article-title><source>Histochem J</source><volume>31</volume><fpage>169</fpage><lpage>174</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10421416</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002476-Tanaka1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tanaka</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Miyamoto</surname><given-names>KI</given-names></name><name><surname>Morita</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Haga</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Segawa</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Regulation of the PepT1 peptide transporter in the rat small intestine in response to 5-fluorouracil-induced injury.</article-title><source>Gastroenterology</source><volume>114</volume><fpage>714</fpage><lpage>723<